{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/614017-demons-and-the-blood-bond","id":614017,"title":"Demons and the Blood Bond.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-03T14:26:45-07:00","id":614017,"title":"Demons and the Blood Bond.","content":"So on the game I run (online) there is a current discussion regarding how the Blood Bond affects Demons.<br /> <br /> I feel like it should affect Demons whoelsale (but they can use Cover to resist it instead of Primum); while others think that it would only affect the Cover who drank from the vampire.<br /> <br /> I <i>know</i> that the errata published says that Demons <i>can</i> be Blood Bonded, but there is absolutely <i>no</i> details or explanation as to how or why. The others think there <i>must</i> be a physical component to blood bond somebody and when a Demon takes Demonic Form, that ceases to be the case in that it's a construct of Primum (which I still think is physical, but they are arguing is more like an Angel being physically manifested).<br /> <br /> I would really like a more definitive answer from Rose or one of the Demon developers, in truth, but anyone's opinions are good here. I don't even need to be right. But I do want to come to a conclusion beyond 'do whatever is right for your game', because the people who decide what's right for the game are disagreeing, so that's not really a good option at the moment. I'm sure I could slam my fist and go, <i>this is how it is</i>, but I don't want to, and even if I did, I wouldn't, not to mention there's a good chance my fellows with the same authority would point and laugh.<br /> <br /> So any help is good help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 08-03-2015, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T02:44:00-07:00","id":614737,"title":"","content":"I'd say - if you feed the Demon the blood while he's in cover - the cover get's bonded. If you feed him while he's in Demon Form (or if he uses partial tansformation to pull out his mouth) then the Demon get's bonded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:56:46-07:00","id":615485,"title":"","content":"I have a character in my game who consumes blood and I have let it be known can be blood bound normally, just like anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T15:53:48-07:00","id":615648,"title":"","content":"In my optinion, it should affect the demon as any other character. Maybe he is immune in demon form due to its inhuman nature (but not to a blood bond he suffered previously in human form). However, a demon should be able to resist as if he were a vampire, with primum or cover instead of blood potency. A denon could also potentially use an exploit to free another demon from a blood bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T21:53:53-07:00","id":615998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/614017-demons-and-the-blood-bond?p=614737#post614737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say - if you feed the Demon the blood while he's in cover - the cover get's bonded. If you feed him while he's in Demon Form (or if he uses partial tansformation to pull out his mouth) then the Demon get's bonded.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of how I plan to treat Disquiet (See Promethean) in Demon, (except Demonic form doesn't acquire Disquiet ever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 08-05-2015, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:42:31-07:00","id":616016,"title":"","content":"I don't give Demons Disquiet at all, in any form, lacking souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:25:47-07:00","id":616050,"title":"","content":"Well technically the Demons (at my table) don't have to act on the Disquiet but not doing so in Cover is considered a Comprise; the Unchained don't have to be mean to the Created but not doing so marks them as distinctly non-human and stand out to the G-M. Attaching the Condition to a Cover is more of a formality; the character can ignore the Condition but the Cover suffers a Comprise.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm evil...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:02:19-07:00","id":616317,"title":"","content":"Covers are basically just masks the demon wears, clothes and appearances he dons at any given moment. If someone attacks the demon while he's acting like James Smith, bus driver, he'll still be showing bruises when taking the form of Jessica Ward, stay-at-home-mom. If a supernatural launches a psychic attack or mind-control effect, it affects the demon, irregardless of what Cover you have up. If a demon is hit by an Arm Wreck tilt, all the Covers will have the Tilt. If the demon has been drugged, all the Covers will be suffering the effect of that drug.<br /> <br /> So, given all that, I would say that, if the demon drinks vitae, then the demon itself is being affected by the addiction and blood bond. No matter the Cover she adopts. Now, <i>acting</i> like you're an addict with a different Cover should be out of character, and thus, a compromise check. But then, this is the reason why demons can perfectly hide their emotions. They could be shaking horribly with withdrawal on the inside, and it won't show on the outside. They'll be in love with the vampire no matter what face they wear, but its not like anything is forcing the demon to act like it in any form except the one Cover they drank from - and it would likely be a compromise check if they didn't act in love in that Cover!<br /> <br /> I think people put too much emphasis on the idea that, when you switch Covers, everything that's happened to the first Cover magically goes away. By the rules, the only things that change when you swap Covers are your appearance and key merits. Everything else stays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T05:03:49-07:00","id":616322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/614017-demons-and-the-blood-bond?p=616050#post616050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well technically the Demons (at my table) don't have to act on the Disquiet but not doing so in Cover is considered a Comprise; the Unchained don't have to be mean to the Created but not doing so marks them as distinctly non-human and stand out to the G-M. Attaching the Condition to a Cover is more of a formality; the character can ignore the Condition but the Cover suffers a Comprise.Yeah, I'm evil...</div> </div> </div> </div> I mostly agree with this! This is how it should work, in my opinion! Though, I am nice enough to let the characters know that not acting that way is a compromise check.<br /> <br /> The only thing I disagree with is that I don't think we should be attaching Conditions - the demon shouldn't be earning Beats by acting in Cover. But that's a personal opinion on the matter, and is open to debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-05-2015, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T04:13:23-07:00","id":617612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/614017-demons-and-the-blood-bond?p=616016#post616016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't give Demons Disquiet at all, in any form, lacking souls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do like to point out that animals ( as far as I understand it in nwod) don't have souls either,hence why I don't let players have animal covers, yet they are still affected by Disquiet just as strongly as humans. Perhaps it could be better to say that demons don't feel the affects of Disquiet due to their techno-spiritual nature?<br /> <br /> For the topic at hand, I handle it like this in my games; Demons in Cover can be subjected to the Blood Bond like any othere human, save for a greater ability to potentially resist it, but while in Demonic Form the affects of the Blood Bond do not apply due to detachment from the body's visceral responses regarding emotion, even the intense false love of the bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-06-2015, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T07:46:32-07:00","id":617753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/614017-demons-and-the-blood-bond?p=616317#post616317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Covers are basically just masks the demon wears, clothes and appearances he dons at any given moment. If someone attacks the demon while he's acting like James Smith, bus driver, he'll still be showing bruises when taking the form of Jessica Ward, stay-at-home-mom. If a supernatural launches a psychic attack or mind-control effect, it affects the demon, irregardless of what Cover you have up. If a demon is hit by an Arm Wreck tilt, all the Covers will have the Tilt. If the demon has been drugged, all the Covers will be suffering the effect of that drug.<br /> <br /> So, given all that, I would say that, if the demon drinks vitae, then the demon itself is being affected by the addiction and blood bond. No matter the Cover she adopts. Now, <i>acting</i> like you're an addict with a different Cover should be out of character, and thus, a compromise check. But then, this is the reason why demons can perfectly hide their emotions. They could be shaking horribly with withdrawal on the inside, and it won't show on the outside. They'll be in love with the vampire no matter what face they wear, but its not like anything is forcing the demon to act like it in any form except the one Cover they drank from - and it would likely be a compromise check if they didn't act in love in that Cover!<br /> <br /> I think people put too much emphasis on the idea that, when you switch Covers, everything that's happened to the first Cover magically goes away. By the rules, the only things that change when you swap Covers are your appearance and key merits. Everything else stays.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the demon is forced to act according to the urges that come from a blood bond in all covers, like any other character suffering a blood bond. That his emotions do not show does not mean that he can resist them. The demon would just obey with a cool poker face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T08:07:01-07:00","id":617776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/614017-demons-and-the-blood-bond?p=617753#post617753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the demon is forced to act according to the urges that come from a blood bond in all covers, like any other character suffering a blood bond. That his emotions do not show does not mean that he can resist them. The demon would just obey with a cool poker face.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. I'm assuming that the vampire is unaware that the demon can switch faces, though.<br /> <br /> Blood bonds work differently in 2e than 1e, so its not quite slavery. What happens in 2e is that it permanently raises your Impression to Perfect and inflict Integrity breaking points for trying to hurt the vampire. This applies to the demon all the time. It also means that, if the vamp want someone under a vinculum to do something, it has to be done through the Social Maneuvering system. If the vampire doesn't know the demon is, well, a demon? Or that the demon can switch faces? The vampire won't know to give orders to Mr/Ms Red in those other faces.<br /> <br /> The demon will always love the vampire, no matter the face, but there is nothing forcing the demon to tell the vamp everything, so I'm assuming that we've got a few secrets here. Keeping secrets is what demons are best at, after all.<br /> <br /> And there's the nature of Covers themselves. While the demon himself is blood bonded, only one Cover is (assuming that Cover wasn't destroyed). Acting blood bonded in the non-bonded Covers surely is a Compromise, and demons, while they love the vamp, aren't suddenly suicidal here. There's a lot of potential for drama and stories here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-06-2015, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}